---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ArticleCard from "../../components/ArticleCard.astro";

const articles = (await getCollection("articles"))
  .filter((article) => article.data.category === "Food Storage")
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf());
---

<BaseLayout title="Food Storage and Stockpiling | Food Supply Crisis Report" description="Evidence-based guides and reporting on household food storage, emergency planning, stockpiling behavior, shelf life and reducing food waste.">
  <section class="hero"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Topic Hub</p><h1>Food Storage & Stockpiling</h1><p>Practical information on food storage, household preparedness, stockpiling behavior, shelf life and sensible emergency planning.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell">
    <h2>Practical preparation without panic buying</h2>
    <p>Household resilience is about keeping a modest supply of familiar food, safe water and the means to prepare meals through a temporary interruption. A good pantry fits the household's normal diet, budget, storage space and special needs. It is used and replenished during ordinary shopping rather than left untouched until food expires.</p>
    <p>Storage advice also has to cover safety. Dry food needs protection from moisture and pests, while power outages require clear decisions about refrigerated and frozen food. Water quantity, container hygiene and local public-health instructions matter as much as the number of cans on a shelf.</p>
    <p>Start with our <a href="/articles/best-non-perishable-foods-30-day-emergency-pantry/">30-day emergency pantry guide</a> for a food inventory and rotation plan, then use the stockpiling and water-storage explainers for the specific issues they cover.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="card-grid">
    {articles.length ? articles.map((article) => (<article class="card"><h2><a href={`/articles/${article.id}/`}>{article.data.title}</a></h2><p>{article.data.description}</p></article>)) : <div class="callout"><strong>Storage coverage:</strong> Upcoming reporting will distinguish practical preparedness from panic buying and explain safe, useful ways to plan household food supplies.</div>}
  </div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
